#
# Counter-example for math:TensorGraphArchitectureConstraint: a
# math:TensorComputationGraph that names no model through math:architectureOf. A lifted
# forward pass anchored to no math:LearnedModel is a graph standing behind nothing, so
# the self-structure reading — an AI reading its own architecture back — has no subject;
# that is the graph-side residue of the front-end's math:UnliftableTensorGraph refusal.
#
# The graph carries the math:computationNode its own min-1 frame requires, so it is NOT
# math:MalformedTensorComputationGraph — the node-presence frame over an EMITTED graph.
# Keeping that frame satisfied is what makes this fixture discriminate the two: this rule
# names the refusal to emit at all, and a fixture missing both would credit the wrong
# class. It fires math:TensorGraphArchitectureConstraint
# (shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent → math:UnliftableTensorGraph).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/tensor-graph-no-architecture/> .

ex:graph a math:TensorComputationGraph ;
    math:computationNode ex:matmul0 .

ex:matmul0 a math:MathematicalObject .
